From 0e81e956b91c0fb00986764f14bcd475e605b267 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 12:09:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] fix(web): footer socials are config-driven and fail
 safe (no dead homepage links)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every footer social icon linked to the bare platform homepage
(instagram.com/, facebook.com/, x.com/, google.com/maps, …) — dead links
that erode trust and leak link equity. Replaced with a SOCIAL_LINKS config
whose href comes from NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_* env vars; an icon renders only when
a real profile URL is set, so a homepage link can never ship and no handle is
invented. Added rel=me for profile verification and documented the vars in
.env.example for the owner to fill in.
